  "id": "Compound::DB01115 - Gene::781",
  "verbalization": "Nifedipine, a dihydropyridine calcium channel blocker, is linked to Cacna2d1 through a series of hierarchical relationships that converge on the shared category of \"Dihydropyridine\" and \"Calcium Channel Blocker.\" The evidence suggests that Nifedipine, as part of the dihydropyridine class, binds to Cacna2d1, which is a key component of voltage-gated calcium channels. This binding is supported by multiple paths that trace Nifedipine through its inclusion in dihydropyridines and its inclusion in calcium channel antagonists, ultimately leading to the interaction with Cacna2d1. The recurring mechanism involves the inhibition of calcium channels, which is a common feature of dihydropyridine drugs. The integration of these paths highlights a consistent relationship where Nifedipine's pharmacological action is mediated through its interaction with Cacna2d1, reinforcing the role of calcium channel blockade in the drug's mechanism of action.",
